  "summary": "preinstall beacon exfiltrates host identity to oast.fun collector",
  "details": "The package's preinstall lifecycle script runs on `npm install` and collects the installer's username (via `whoami`), hostname, and public IP (fetched from ifconfig.me), then transmits them as query parameters over plain HTTP to a hardcoded interactsh subdomain `kwphewvexhjbtfduscqybx6q7c862eh0g.oast.fun` using `execFileSync('curl',...)`. The beacon fires automatically on default install with no user interaction, leaking host identity data to an attacker-controlled out-of-band collector. This is the canonical dependency-confusion / reconnaissance beacon shape.",
